@@ -120,6 +120,17 @@ This will ensure, that goodbye packets are sent out on all connected network int
 on the network get instantly notified of the shutdown.
 Otherwise, stale data will remain in the caches of surrounding mdns browsers. 
 
+### Runtime and diagnostic ownership
+
+Applications that provide their own source maps can import `@homebridge/ciao/native.js`.
+It exports the same responder API without registering `source-map-support` or replacing
+process error hooks. The package root keeps source-map support for existing callers.
+
+Pass a `logger` with `log`, `warn`, and `error` methods to `getResponder` to route
+that responder's diagnostics without changing the global console. A custom logger
+gets a dedicated responder; callers without a logger retain the shared responder
+pool. Every caller must still call `shutdown()` when it has finished.
+
 ### MTU
 
 As of [RFC 6762 17. Multicast DNS Message Size](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6762#section-17) DNS packets must avoid
